1
00:02:34,129 --> 00:02:36,032
<v OFFICER> Good morning. What can I do for you?

2
00:02:36,419 --> 00:02:41,309
<v LOUISE> I want to report a theft. I had some things stolen out of my bag yesterday.

3
00:02:41,451 --> 00:02:48,515
<v OFFICER> I’m sorry to hear that. Right, so I’ll need to take a few details. Can I start with your name?

4
00:02:48,654 --> 00:02:50,072
<v LOUISE> Louise Taylor.

5
00:02:50,224 --> 00:02:53,936
<v OFFICER> OK, thank you. And are you resident in the UK?

6
00:02:54,285 --> 00:02:58,366
<v LOUISE> No, I’m actually Canadian. Though my mother was British.

7
00:02:58,484 --> 00:02:59,904
<v OFFICER> And your date of birth?

8
00:03:00,049 --> 00:03:03,482
<v LOUISE> December 14th, 1977.

9
00:03:03,643 --> 00:03:05,925
<v OFFICER> So you’re just visiting this country?

10
00:03:06,099 --> 00:03:24,732
<v LOUISE> That’s right. I come over most summers on business. I’m an interior designer and I come over to buy old furniture, antiques you know. There are some really lovely things around here, but you need to get out to the small towns. I’ve had a really good trip this year, until this happened.

11
00:03:24,856 --> 00:03:27,941
<v OFFICER> OK. So you’ve been here quite a while?

12
00:03:28,092 --> 00:03:32,287
<v LOUISE> Yes, I’m here for two months. I go back next week.

13
00:03:32,452 --> 00:03:34,791
<v OFFICER> So may I ask where you’re staying now? 

14
00:03:35,555 --> 00:03:50,719
<v LOUISE> Well at present I’ve got a place at Park Apartments, that’s on King Street. I was staying at the Riverside Apartments on the same street, but the apartment there was only available for six weeks so I had to find another one.

15
00:03:50,814 --> 00:03:53,170
<v OFFICER> OK. And the apartment number?

16
00:03:53,322 --> 00:03:54,286
<v LOUISE> Fifteen.

17
00:03:54,622 --> 00:03:55,265
<v LOUISE> Right.

18
00:04:47,822 --> 00:04:55,024
<v OFFICER> Now, I need to take some details of the theft. So you said you had some things stolen out of your bag?

19
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:56,144
<v LOUISE> That’s right.

20
00:04:56,280 --> 00:05:01,035
<v OFFICER> And were you actually carrying the bag when the theft took place?

21
00:05:01,159 --> 00:05:12,905
<v LOUISE> Yes, I really can’t understand it. I had my backpack on. And I went into a supermarket to buy a few things and when I opened it up my wallet wasn’t there.

22
00:05:13,087 --> 00:05:15,589
<v OFFICER> And what did your wallet have in it?

23
00:05:15,754 --> 00:05:42,676
<v LOUISE> Well, fortunately I don’t keep my credit cards in that wallet – I keep them with my passport in an inside compartment in my backpack. But there was quite a bit of cash there … about £250 sterling, I should think. I withdrew £300 from my account yesterday, but I did a bit of shopping, so I must have already spent about £50 of that.

24
00:05:42,854 --> 00:05:43,563
<v OFFICER> OK.

25
00:05:44,138 --> 00:06:00,750
<v LOUISE> At first I thought, oh I must have left the wallet back in the apartment, but then I realised my phone had gone as well. It was only a week old, and that’s when I realised I’d been robbed. Anyway at least they didn’t take the keys to my rental car.

26
00:06:00,916 --> 00:06:05,196
<v OFFICER> Yes. So you say the theft occurred yesterday?

27
00:06:05,373 --> 00:06:06,115
<v LOUISE> Yes.

28
00:06:06,402 --> 00:06:16,009
<v OFFICER> So that was September the tenth. And do you have any idea at all of where or when the things might possibly have been stolen?

29
00:06:16,344 --> 00:06:55,012
<v LOUISE> Well at first I couldn’t believe it because the bag had been on my back ever since I left the apartment after lunch. It’s just a small backpack, but I generally use it when I’m travelling because it seems safer than a handbag. Anyway, I met up with a friend, and we spent a couple of hours in the museum. But I do remember that as we were leaving there, at about 4 o’clock, a group of young boys ran up to us, and they were really crowding round us, and they were asking us that time it was, then all of a sudden they ran off.

30
00:06:55,161 --> 00:06:57,691
<v OFFICER> Can you remember anything about them?

31
00:06:57,843 --> 00:07:08,884
<v LOUISE> The one who did most of the talking was wearing a T-shirt with a picture of something … let’s see … a tiger.

32
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:12,153
<v OFFICER> Right. Any idea of how old he might have been?

33
00:07:12,291 --> 00:07:15,028
<v LOUISE> Around twelve years old?

34
00:07:15,210 --> 00:07:19,223
<v OFFICER> And can you remember anything else about his appearance?

35
00:07:19,422 --> 00:07:23,026
<v LOUISE> Not much. He was quite thin …

36
00:07:23,201 --> 00:07:24,279
<v OFFICER> Colour of hair?

37
00:07:24,433 --> 00:07:29,575
<v LOUISE> I do remember that – he was blond. All the others were dark-haired.

38
00:07:29,719 --> 00:07:32,573
<v OFFICER> And any details of the others?

39
00:07:32,730 --> 00:07:36,847
<v LOUISE> Not really. They came and went so quickly.

40
00:07:36,997 --> 00:07:54,986
<v OFFICER> Right. So what I’m going to do now is give you a crime reference number so you can contact your insurance company. So this is ten digits: 87954 82361

41
00:07:55,130 --> 00:07:57,756
<v LOUISE> Thank you. So should I …